since he made his debut in 1988 venom  has become one of spider-man's deadliest  and most well known foes so well known  in fact that you're probably already  familiar with most of the facts about  his origin from the alien costume that  Spidey picked up in secret Wars to his  defeat by a church bell and even his  appearance in the classic maximum  carnage video game you might think you  know it all dig a little deeper though  and you might find a few facts that you  didn't know about venom venom a David  Goyer film while Tom Hardy will be  taking on the role of venom in the  characters first major solo film it's  hardly the first time someone has tried  to bring venom to the big screen for his  own movie there were plans for a  spin-off series after Eddie Brock made  his appearance as one of the villains in  2007 spider-man 3 but 10 years earlier  New Line Cinema was making a serious  effort to make venom the motion picture  happen while it never happened it  boasted a screenplay by David s Goyer  and was rumored to have Dolph Lundgren  in talks to star not a bad choice when  you consider how often artists of the  90s drew Eddie Brock to look like an  even more jacked version of Ivan Drago  Gore would eventually break through into  superhero films as the writer of 1998's  Blade and its sequels and would go on to  provide the scripts for Batman Begins  Man of Steel and dawn of Justice what  could have been truth in journalism  if big-budget superhero movies aren't  your thing you don't need to wait to see  an interesting live-action take on venom  thanks to Joe Lynch's truth and  journalism  released as a fan film in 2013 the  documentary style movie follows  disgraced photojournalist Eddie B as he  makes his way through the streets of New  York finding and occasionally  manufacturing salacious news stories  needless to say it turns out that  Eddie's hiding an even bigger secret  spoiler warning it's a weird symbiote  monster from space who eats people even  though most viewers know exactly who  Eddie B is from the first frame the big  reveal of venom at the end is well-done  intense with ryan Kwanten of True Blood  Fame doing a great job of playing Brock  as an amoral opportunist if you've never  seen it it's well worth 20 minutes of  your time and like all Marvel movies  make sure you stick around after the  credits venom vs. number 7 in the 1990s  venom was easily one of Marvel's single  most popular characters for a pretty  obvious reason he was basically Frank  Castle Plus Peter Parker with a mouth  full of teeth so long and sharp that  even Wolverine thought it was a bit much  he was so popular in fact that from 1993  to 1998 there was a new issue of venom  on the stands every single month without  missing a beat those issues just never  managed to get past number six rather  than being a single comic that ran from  number one to number 60 Venom's ongoing  adventures were broken into a staggering  17 different series that ran back to  back to back to back to Bell you get the  idea  it started in February of 93 with venom  lethal protector and ran through  separation anxiety sinner takes all  license to kill and a dozen other books  before finally wrapping up with the  appropriately named venom the finale in  January of 1998 as for why they didn't  just keep lethal protector going well  that's simple everyone knows that a  number one issue is more valuable for  collectors right and what's better than  one number one seventeen number ones  wait what do you mean that's not how  supply and demand works the thin line  between love and hate it was bad enough  when Peter Parker discovered that his  black costume was a living creature  hell-bent on controlling his body but it  got even worse when the symbiote joined  up with Eddie Brock whose hatred of  Parker only amplified the aliens  resentment after being rejected it  doesn't take a lot of analysis to see  the subtext in that relationship the  rejection the jealousy the new partner  picked up on the rebound for all intents  and purposes the symbiote is reacting  like a scorned lover  it isn't just subtext it's the whole  point of one of the greatest venom  stories of all time an amazing  spider-man number 317 Eddie Brock  challenges Peter to a one-on-one fight  to the death alone and completely  outmatched in terms of strength Peter  makes the desperate move of stripping  off his costume and seducing the venom  suit with the proportionate sexiness of  a spider  if the subtext had been difficult to see  before then the sight of Peter Parker  standing on a beach and tiny Underpants  offering up his body put an exclamation  point on the whole thing it actually  worked too but the symbiotes  relationship with Eddie turned out to be  too deep to drop all at once leaving him  passed out on the beach and his  underpants covered in a viscous ooze and  who hasn't been there after a bad  breakup  Superman smacked down while he's come  pretty close on several occasions venom  has never been able to truly defeat  spider-man once and for all he did  however beat the living heck outta  Superman so he's got that going for him  it happened in a follow up to the world  colliding DC vs. Marvel crossover to his  credit Superman manages to hold his own  but you  think that a guy who can shoot heat  lasers out of his eyes and make a sonic  boom by clapping his hands would  probably have a pretty easy time  fighting someone whose major weaknesses  are loud noises and fire and yet once  venom flies into a rage he not only goes  toe to toe with the last Son of Krypton  he also beats up Superman and spider-man  at the same time the only reason the  good guys are able to pull off the win  is the intervention of a third character  access an obscure goofball who's jointly  owned by Marvel and DC and apparently  has the deus ex machina powers of both  companies rolled into one an extra sting  in the tail if you're familiar with Mac  Gargan it's probably from his original  villainous identity the Scorpion  introduced in 1964 Guardian was a  crooked Private Eye hired by Jay jonah  Jameson to dig up dirt on everyone's  favorite web slinger when that didn't  work out triple j decided that it would  probably be a good idea to do some mad  science on him and give him a robotic  scorpion tail instead this was not in  fact a good idea in 2005 however Gargan  decided to go in a bit of a different  direction  when eddie brock found jesus he decided  to give up the symbiote and auction it  off to the highest bidder Gargan wound  up with it became the new venom and not  only did he fight spider-man in this  identity he actually replaced him by  joining up with Norman Osborn's  government-approved team of Dark  Avengers as Freddy the combination of  another villains healing powers and a  chance encounter with an old symbiote  caused a reaction that gave him his  powers back and more it turned him into  a sort of color and verted version of  venom who had the ability to cure others  of symbiote related afflictions and he  fought against crime as wait for it  anti-venom  Viva venom variety Eddie Brock and Mac  Gargan are the most well known Venom's  but they're not the only characters to  take on the identity in recent years  it's bounced around the Marvel Universe  so much that it seems like everyone's  had a shot even Groot here's a quick  rundown Flash Thompson who first  appeared back in the 60s as the high  school bully who constantly picked on  puny Parker before eventually becoming  his friend lost his legs while serving  in the Army in Iraq in 2011 his heroic  ideals in history of valor and service  made him the military's ideal candidate  for a program designed to create a new  kind of super soldier agent venom he was  bonded to the symbiote for 48 hours at a  time to keep him from losing control and  served as a member of both the Secret  Avengers and guardians of the galaxy  before losing the symbiotes back to  Eddie Brock and becoming wait for it  again  agent anti-venom if that wasn't weird  enough Thompson's time serving alongside  the Guardians also involved a mishap  that saw not just group being taken over  but rocket too and if you've ever been  startled by a raccoon by your trash cans  just imagine how bad it would be if he  had a laser gun and was also bonded with  the super-powered alien it doesn't end  there though over the years the symbiote  has briefly bonded with Deadpool  Wolverine Captain Marvel a villain named  Lee price Drax the destroyer Doctor  Octopus when he was living in Peter  Parker's body another version of  Wolverine and a kid who became venom  because he wanted girls to write  fanfiction about him no really and  that's just in the regular Marvel  continuity if you expand it out - what  if stories an alternate universe as  Venom's been well pretty much everyone  from the Punisher to Galactus the  Devourer of worlds but believe it or not  that's not the weirdest one  beware the V Rex if you go into it  looking to find out what happened to  your favorite superheroes mark Miller  and Steve McNiven old man Logan is a  pretty huge bummer focused on an older  Wolverine and a blinded Hawkeye driving  across a devastated America that's been  carved up by supervillains it devotes a  lot of pages to revealing how the heroes  of the Marvel Universe died or worse if  you like venom though buckle up as  Wolverine and Hawkeye drive spider-man's  old car through a chunk of the Midwest  that's been taken over by the dinosaurs  of the Savage Land they accidentally get  on the wrong side of a Tyrannosaurus Rex  that's bonded with the Venom symbiote to  create Earth's perfect killing machine  maybe next time drive a car without its  own arch enemy thanks for watching click  the looper icon to subscribe to our  youtube channel plus check out all this  cool stuff we know you'll love to  you
 

